ions.\n- It is consistent with the acquiring fund's investment objectives and policies.\n\nThe findings must be documented and reported to the acquiring fund's board, which oversees the adviser's process.\n\n**Fund of funds investment agreement:** Generally required in writing. It typically covers:\n- Acknowledgment of the rule's conditions and limits on control.\n- Voting and redemption arrangements.\n- Sales-load and fee terms.\n- Mechanisms for the acquired fund to reject or limit investments.\n\nConfirm the precise conditions, including board-approval and notice requirements, against current Rule 12d1-4 and SEC guidance before relying on this summary.","ttft_ms":2559,"type":"result","duration_ms":3446,"uuid":"df363623-d090-4c94-a66f-d152abcb7aeb","ttft_stream_ms":856,"time_to_request_ms":81,"first_content_frame_ms":856,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
